00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:16.140
which probably is a pity.

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:19.380
But since I'm making a difference

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:23.070
and hopefully helping to make
the world a better place,

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:25.560
then I can live with it.

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.620
Do you think we shouldn't
have private jets?

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:29.453
No.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.150 position:56%
I mean, I think for some businesses,

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:35.340 position:59%
it's almost necessary, especially now.

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:39.390
Post pandemic, the air travel is,

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:43.230
you get flights canceled,
you get flights delayed,

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.030
you can't make your connection.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.920 position:66%
Are you gonna tell some of the celebrities

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:48.630
and some of the leaders
who follow your work

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:49.950
and you get to have audiences with

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:50.970
or they have audiences with you

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:54.120 position:63%
to stop using the private jets, the PJs?

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.826
No, I'm not going to tell them.

00:21:55.826 --> 00:21:58.077
People need to, you know,

00:21:58.077 --> 00:22:02.820 position:64%
I have never been one to confront people,

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:05.070
because I think the only way

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:08.250
that you can create change
in some of these people

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:09.690
is not to argue with them,

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:12.330
not to tell them what they
should or shouldn't do,

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:13.890
but to reach the heart.

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.510
And how do you reach the heart?

00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:17.163
By telling stories.

00:22:18.030 --> 00:22:21.330
And this one story, which
I'll share with you now

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:24.540 position:61%
is a CEO of a big international company

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:27.750
and he was telling me that
for the last eight years,

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:30.390 position:66%
he's been really trying to get his company

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:32.378
to have ethical practices

00:22:32.378 --> 00:22:35.910
in all the different
countries for three reasons.

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:38.190 position:56%
One, seeing the writing on the wall,

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.200
using up natural resources,

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:43.470
in some cases faster than
nature can replenish them.

00:22:43.470 --> 00:22:45.810
Secondly, consumer pressure.

00:22:45.810 --> 00:22:48.090 position:59%
People who can afford it are beginning

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:50.970
to demand products that
have been made ethically.

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:52.980 position:58%
But he said, "What tipped the balance

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.891
was my little girl of 8,

00:22:54.891 --> 00:22:57.480
came back from school
one day and she said,

00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:00.870
'Daddy, they tell me
that what you're doing

00:23:00.870 --> 00:23:02.910
is hurting the planet.

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.800
That's not true, is it, Daddy?

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:06.750
'Cause it's my planet.'"

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:09.210
Dr. Goodall, thank you
very much for your time.

00:23:09.210 --> 00:23:10.260
Well, thank you too.

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:13.350
And just remember, every
single day we live,

00:23:13.350 --> 00:23:15.810
every one of us makes an impact

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:19.050
and we get to choose what
sort of impact we make.

00:23:19.050 --> 00:23:21.673
A very powerful message
to end on. Thank you.

00:23:21.673 --> 00:23:22.811
Thank you.

00:23:22.811 --> 00:23:25.140 position:63%
And thank you so much for being with us.

00:23:25.140 --> 00:23:28.023
Until we meet again,
take care and goodbye.

